==English==
{{Webster}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|bespeken|lang=enm}}, {{term|bispeken|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} *{{term||bespecan|lang=ang}}, {{term|besprecan||to speak about, speak against, accuse of, claim at law, complain|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|bisprekanan|to discuss, blame|lang=en}}, equivalent to {{prefix|be|speak}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|bespeke||to beseech, speak or negotiate with|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|besprekke||to discuss|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|bespreken||to discuss, review, debate|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|besprechen||to discuss, review, talk about|lang=de}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA| [bɪˈspiːk]}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|bespeaks|bespeaking|'''[[bespoke]]''' or '''[[bespake]]''' (archaic)|'''[[bespoken]]''' or '''[[bespoke]]''' (archaic)}}

# {{transitive}} To [[speak]] about; tell of; [[relate]]; [[discuss]].
#*'''2006''', Janet Jaymes, ''Dirty Laundry: A Memoir'':
#*: But to '''bespeak''' of a love, heavily weighed upon a heart, toward someone opposing those sentiments encourages foolish and embarrassing repercussions he will never know about.
# {{transitive}} To speak for beforehand; [[engage]] in advance; make arrangements for; [[order]] or [[reserve]] [[in advance]].
#: ''to '''bespeak''' a seat in a theatre''
# {{transitive}} To [[stipulate]], [[solicit]], [[ask for]], or [[request]], as in a favour.
#: ''to '''bespeak''' a calm hearing''
#: ''I '''bespeak''' your patience in advance.''
# {{transitive|archaic}} To [[forbode]]; [[foretell]].
# {{transitive|archaic|poetic}} To speak to; [[address]].
#: ''He thus the queen '''bespoke'''.'' &mdash; Dryden.
# {{transitive}} To [[betoken]]; [[show]]; [[indicate]]; [[foretell]]; [[suggest]].
#: ''[They] '''bespoke''' dangers . . . in order to scare the allies.'' &mdash; Swift.
#: ''This act '''bespeaks''' his kindness.''
# {{intransitive}} To [[speak up]] or [[speak out|out]]; [[exclaim]]; speak.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|bespeaker}}
* {{l|en|bespeaking}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[request]] for a specific performance; a [[benefit]] performance, by a patron.
#* '''1839''', Charles Dickens, ''[[w:Nicholas Nickleby|Nicholas Nickleby]]''
#*: "By the bye, I've been thinking of bringing out that piece of yours on her '''bespeak''' night."
#*: "When?", asked Nicholas.
#*: "The night of her '''bespeak'''. Her benefit night. When her friends and patrons '''bespeak''' the play."
#*: "Oh! I understand", replied Nicholas.

